{
 "_doc": [
  "Two one-day surveys of the Thenpennai, transcribed from the reports filed before the NGT (Southern Zone): the joint committee's 12-point sampling of 9 and 10 September 2020 (O.A. 111 of 2020) and the CPCB, KSPCB and TNPCB joint sampling of six points on 28 October 2024 (O.A. 14 of 2025). Every value is as printed; tables were read from the page images.",
  "Positions. The 2024 report prints coordinates (its Table 2); the 2020 report's coordinate column is blank on the printed page (the PDF's text layer carries figures that do not match the places, so they are not used). 2020 points are therefore placed by name: the 2024 coordinate where the same place was sampled in 2024, else a named OSM or TNGIS place, snapped to the mapped river where the point is a river point ('snap': true). Bengaluru's four lake outfalls sit at their lakes' centres.",
  "2024 Table 2 quirk: the longitude column for points iv to vi is offset by one row (three longitudes printed against two latitudes in sequence); they are paired here in flow order, so 'Kelavarapalli outfall' takes 77.875117 and 'Mitteganahalli bridge' 77.876822. Marked for review.",
  "'BDL' and 'ND' are the report's own cells (below detection limit, not detected). Coliform counts in the 2024 table are printed as 'n x 10^k' and expanded here.",
  "Units unless stated: mg/L; conductivity µS/cm; turbidity NTU; coliforms MPN/100ml; SAR meq/L. 2020 Table 1 'FC' column is fecal coliform."
 ],
